#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""unsay — unspeak ALOUD so a BLAST survivor rides again.

aloud *names* the blast survivor that later restated the new default
(ALOUD) versus the one that stayed omitted (MUTE). Naming is not a
witness. unsay emits the unified diff that deletes the explicit
new-default argument (ALOUD → TACIT) so the site rides again. Optionally
`--pin` writes the new default at MUTE sites (MUTE → SHADOW).

    ALOUD  --emit deletes the spoken new-default arg
    MUTE   --pin inserts the inherited new-default arg
    PRE    already spoke at the blast — not unsaid
    LATE   never rode the blast — not unsaid
    FOSSIL restates the *old* value — not unsaid

The patch is the witness that the fate was real. A leftover-name search
or `rg presentThreshold: 0.45` cannot tell ALOUD from PRE from LATE;
unsay only rewrites ALOUD.
"""
